==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/uːf/|/ʊf/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|ūf|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/uf/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-oof.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːf|ʊf|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
An onomatopoeia. Similar to {{cog|nl|oef}} and {{cog|de|uff}}.
<!--The verb sense is from a sound effect used in [[point-of-view]] video games when a character dies.-->

The usage of this term on the Internet was popularized by the game platform {{w|Roblox}}.

====Interjection====
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} {{n-g|A sound [[mimicking]] the loss of air, as if someone's [[solar plexus]] had just been struck.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=5 Jun 1989|journal=The Canberra Times|location=Australia Captial Territory|page=10|column=2|text=Whap, Biff, '''Ooooof''', Sock, Pow, Zok! ''Batman'' is back. Gotham City is again leaving its law and order in the hands of a man who wears plastic underpants over his tights.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} {{synonym of|en|ouch||expressing sympathy at another's pain, shock at a high price, etc.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2017|title=Getting Over It with Bennett Foddy
|passage="'''Oof''', you just lost a lot of progress. That's a real frustration, a real punch in the gut."}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A sound made in pain, as when [[expel]]ling air after being struck.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1966|author=James Workman|title=The Mad Emperor|publisher=Scripts|location=Melbourne, Sydney|page=33|passage=The soldier on the ground clutched his head and then his stomach and gave an "'''oof'''" of pain.}}
# {{lb|en|Internet}} Something [[cringeworthy]], or which arouses [[disappointment]], often used in conjunction with the qualifier ''[[big]]''.
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=27 July 2022|author=Eleni Thomas|title=Roblox is removing iconic “oof” sound after copyright issues|work=Dexerto|url=https://www.dexerto.com/gaming/roblox-removing-iconic-oof-sound-copyright-issues-1884500/|text=Fans were quick to express their disappointment at the removal of what has now become an iconic sound in the gaming space. The audio is trending on Twitter under #SaveTheOOF and Big '''Oof'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|1=en|date=22 September 2022|author=Vinepair Staff|title=The Cocktail College Podcast: How to Make the Perfect El Diablo|work=The Cocktail College Podcast|url=https://vinepair.com/cocktail-college/el-diablo/|text=That actually hits me home because I used to drink tequila sunrises when I first started drinking. So that’s an '''oof'''.}}

